description:
The subscribe_events() SSE framing loop maintains scan_from = old_len.saturating_sub(3) and re-starts the delimiter search from that position after each chunk append. The comment explains the invariant: 3 bytes back covers the longest incomplete delimiter prefix that can straddle a chunk boundary, specifically the prefix of the CRLF variant 
 (which is the start of 

). A contributor might 'simplify' this to always scan from 0, which is correct but O(n^2) in buffer size and pathological for large slow streams. They might also change the 3 to 1 to save one comparison, which would miss the CRLF case and produce a framing bug. The value 3 is derived directly from the longest incomplete multi-byte delimiter prefix. Do not change it.
